---
import "../styles/global.css";
import RetroKeyboard from "../components/RetroKeyboard.astro";
import { Linkedin, Github } from "@lucide/astro";
---

<html lang="en">
    <head>
        <meta charset="utf-8" />
        <link rel="icon" type="image/svg+xml" href="/favicon.svg" />
        <link rel="icon" href="/favicon.ico" />
        <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width" />
        <meta name="generator" content={Astro.generator} />
        <link rel="preconnect" href="https://fonts.googleapis.com" />
        <link rel="preconnect" href="https://fonts.gstatic.com" crossorigin />
        <link
            href="https://fonts.googleapis.com/css2?family=Lato:wght@400;700&family=Noto+Sans:wght@400;600;700&display=swap"
            rel="stylesheet"
        />
        <title>About - Andrew Hall</title>
    </head>
    <body class="font-sans bg-orange-100 text-amber-950 min-h-screen">
        <main class="max-w-4xl mx-auto px-8 py-12">
            <!-- Navigation -->
            <nav class="mb-12">
                <a
                    href="/"
                    class="text-amber-600 hover:text-amber-800 transition-colors"
                    >← Back to Home</a
                >
            </nav>

            <!-- Header -->
            <header class="mb-12">
                <h1 class="font-mono text-5xl font-bold mb-4">About</h1>
            </header>

            <!-- Content Section -->
            <section class="space-y-8">
                <div>
                    <p class="text-lg leading-relaxed mb-4">
                        There is often a perceived divide between the creative
                        and the technical. I grew up in an environment where
                        engineering rigour and artistic expression were
                        constantly overlapping, so I never saw that divide. I
                        learned early on that structure and creativity are not
                        opposing forces; they are partners.
                    </p>
                    <p class="text-lg leading-relaxed">
                        This duality defines my work. Whether it's an
                        interactive 3D experience, a mobile app or a complex
                        financial platform, the philosophy remains the same: the
                        best technical solutions aren't just functionally
                        correct; they have to feel right to the people using
                        them.
                    </p>
                </div>

                <!-- Keyboard -->
                <div class="flex justify-center mt-12 lg:mt-16">
                    <RetroKeyboard />
                </div>

                <div>
                    <h2 class="font-mono text-2xl font-bold mb-4">
                        From economics to engineering
                    </h2>
                    <p class="text-lg leading-relaxed mb-4">
                        Software is an investment. Coming from a background in
                        economics rather than pure computer science, I view
                        development through a distinct lens: one of ROI,
                        opportunity cost, and resource allocation.
                    </p>
                    <p class="text-lg leading-relaxed">
                        In an industry obsessed with the "new," it is easy to
                        over-engineer. The economic mindset shifts the question
                        from "Can we build this?" to "Should we?" It brings a
                        discipline to the process, ensuring that technical
                        complexity is always justified by clear business value.
                    </p>
                </div>

                <div>
                    <h2 class="font-mono text-2xl font-bold mb-4">
                        Evidence over intuition
                    </h2>
                    <p class="text-lg leading-relaxed mb-4">
                        This focus on value drives a rejection of guesswork.
                        True technical leadership isn't just about executing a
                        roadmap; it is about interrogating the problem.
                    </p>
                    <p class="text-lg leading-relaxed mb-4">
                        Building the right thing requires closing the feedback
                        loop between product vision and technical reality. But
                        evidence isn't limited to API logs and retention
                        metrics; it includes the voice of the market itself.
                    </p>
                    <p class="text-lg leading-relaxed">
                        Great products emerge when engineers are connected
                        directly with customers. By bringing market research and
                        user feedback right into the design and engineering
                        space, we drive the entire team to think commercially.
                        This ensures we aren't just solving abstract logic
                        puzzles, but solving validated business problems.
                    </p>
                </div>

                <div>
                    <h2 class="font-mono text-2xl font-bold mb-4">
                        Velocity versus direction
                    </h2>
                    <p class="text-lg leading-relaxed mb-4">
                        This rigourous approach is vital in the current AI
                        revolution. The democratisation of development is
                        exciting because it allows ideas to be tested faster
                        than ever before. But speed is not the same as
                        direction.
                    </p>
                    <p class="text-lg leading-relaxed mb-4">
                        When code is cheap, judgment becomes expensive. It is
                        critical to distinguish between a distracting experiment
                        and a viable feature. AI is a powerful accelerator, but
                        it requires a steady hand on the wheel to ensure rapid
                        prototyping creates a coherent path forward, rather than
                        a pile of disconnected tech debt.
                    </p>
                </div>

                <div>
                    <h2 class="font-mono text-2xl font-bold mb-4">
                        Strategy in motion
                    </h2>
                    <p class="text-lg leading-relaxed mb-4">
                        Ultimately, strategy cannot survive in a silo. It has to
                        live in the daily operations of the team.
                    </p>
                    <p class="text-lg leading-relaxed mb-4">
                        Bridging the gap between the boardroom and the IDE is
                        essential. Business goals must translate into clear
                        technical requirements, and technical constraints must
                        inform business strategy. It isn't enough to just hand
                        down a vision; we have to build the team, the culture,
                        and the operational systems required to deliver it.
                    </p>
                    <p class="text-lg leading-relaxed">
                        I am here to ensure that the vision isn't just a slide
                        deck, but a scalable, working reality.
                    </p>
                </div>
            </section>

            <!-- Footer Section -->
            <footer
                class="mt-16 pt-8 border-t-2 border-amber-950/20 text-center"
            >
                <div class="flex gap-4 justify-center items-center flex-wrap">
                    <a
                        href="https://www.linkedin.com/in/a-hall2"
                        target="_blank"
                        rel="noopener noreferrer"
                        class="inline-flex items-center gap-2 px-6 py-3 bg-amber-600 text-orange-100 font-semibold rounded hover:bg-amber-700 transition-colors"
                    >
                        <Linkedin size={20} />
                        LinkedIn
                    </a>
                    <a
                        href="https://github.com/andytango"
                        target="_blank"
                        rel="noopener noreferrer"
                        class="inline-flex items-center gap-2 px-6 py-3 bg-amber-600 text-orange-100 font-semibold rounded hover:bg-amber-700 transition-colors"
                    >
                        <Github size={20} />
                        GitHub
                    </a>
                </div>
            </footer>
        </main>
        <!-- Cloudflare Web Analytics -->
        <script
            defer
            src="https://static.cloudflareinsights.com/beacon.min.js"
            data-cf-beacon='{"token": "9dde7d572a9c4cd6b72afe90def4d74f"}'
        ></script><!-- End Cloudflare Web Analytics -->
    </body>
</html>
